{
  "descriptions": {
    "sweIntern": "As a Software Development Engineer Intern, you will design, implement and test features for services used by millions of customers. You will write code in Java or Python, take part in code reviews, debug issues, and work with your mentor and team to deliver a project by the end of the internship. Basic qualifications: currently enrolled in a bachelor's or master's degree in computer science or a related field, experience with at least one programming language such as Java, C++ or Python, and familiarity with data structures and algorithms.",
    "seniorSde": "We are looking for a Senior Software Development Engineer to lead the design of highly available distributed systems. You will own the architecture of services that handle millions of requests per second, mentor engineers, drive operational excellence, and work with product managers to define the roadmap. Requirements: 5+ years of professional software development, experience designing large-scale systems, and strong coding skills in Java, Go or Python.",
    "dataAnalystCollab": "We are looking for a Data Analyst to join our analytics team. You will write SQL queries against our data warehouse, build dashboards in Tableau, and analyze A/B test results to measure the impact of product changes. You will partner closely with software engineers and product managers to define metrics and instrument new features. Requirements: 2+ years of experience with SQL and Excel, working knowledge of statistics and regression, experience with Python or R, and strong communication skills to present insights to stakeholders.",
    "dataAnalystMentionsEngineers": "You will work alongside software engineers, product managers and designers on our checkout team. Partner with software engineers to instrument events and with product managers to define success metrics for each launch. Day to day you will write SQL, maintain Tableau dashboards, and run statistical analysis on experiments, then share insights with the team. Experience working with software engineers in an agile environment is a plus.",
    "sweBackend": "Backend Software Engineer: build and operate REST APIs and microservices in TypeScript and Node.js, deploy to AWS using CI/CD pipelines, write unit tests, take part in code reviews and on-call rotations, and debug production issues in distributed systems. Experience with Git, Java or Python and React is a plus.",
    "apmCapitalOne": "As an Associate Product Manager you will work with engineering, design and business partners to define customer problems, write requirements, prioritize the backlog, and launch features for our banking app. You will use data to measure the success of each launch. Strong analytical skills and a bachelor's degree are required.",
    "technicalPm": "The Technical Product Manager owns the roadmap for our developer platform APIs. You will gather requirements from internal engineering teams, write specifications, prioritize the backlog, and coordinate launches with engineers. A background in software development is helpful.",
    "biDeveloper": "Build and maintain Power BI dashboards and data models, write SQL to transform data from the warehouse, define KPI metrics with business stakeholders, and support self-service analytics across the organization.",
    "financialAnalyst": "The Financial Analyst will build monthly forecasts and budget variance reports, write SQL queries to pull data from the general ledger, maintain Excel models and Tableau dashboards for leadership, and analyze key performance metrics to support business decisions.",
    "businessAnalyst": "The Business Analyst will gather requirements from business stakeholders, document current and future processes, analyze data in Excel and SQL to find opportunities, and present recommendations to leadership.",
    "generic": "We are seeking a motivated team member who thrives in a fast-paced environment. The ideal candidate has excellent communication skills, strong attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities. Responsibilities include supporting day-to-day operations, collaborating with cross-functional teams, and contributing to process improvements. A bachelor's degree is preferred.",
    "groupPm": "Lead a team of product managers responsible for our payments products. Set product strategy and the roadmap, align executives across business units, and coach and hire product managers.",
    "marketingAnalytics": "The Marketing Manager will plan campaigns, write SQL queries to pull campaign data, maintain Tableau dashboards and Excel reports, run A/B tests on email and landing pages, and analyze conversion metrics and statistics to decide where to spend the budget.",
    "newGradNurse": "New graduate Registered Nurse for our medical-surgical unit. Provide safe, patient-centered care, administer medications, monitor vital signs, document in the EHR, and communicate changes in condition to the charge nurse and providers. Requires a current RN license and BLS certification.",
    "consultant": "As a Consultant you will work on client engagements, analyze business problems, build recommendations and present findings in slides and workshops. Strong problem solving, communication and teamwork skills are required.",
    "securityIntern": "Security Engineer Intern: help monitor alerts in our SIEM, investigate phishing reports, review firewall rules and run vulnerability scans with the security team. Coursework in networking, Linux and cybersecurity is preferred.",
    "dataScientist": "Data Scientist: build statistical models and run experiments to improve credit decisions, write SQL and Python, and present insights and recommendations to business partners.",
    "personalBanker": "Personal Banker: help customers open accounts, recommend products that fit their needs, resolve service issues, and build long-term relationships in a busy branch.",
    "uxDesigner": "UX Designer: run usability testing, turn research into wireframes and Figma prototypes, contribute to our design system, and partner with product managers and engineers to ship accessible experiences."
  },
